FINDINGS

- [P2] Visual-mode arrow keys do not work in the real terminal input path. `src/terminal_app.rs:436` processes terminal input byte-by-byte, and `src/terminal_app.rs:469` dispatches `UiKey::Esc` immediately unless `defer_escape_key()` is true. That helper only defers for prompt mode or insert-mode right-pane input at `src/terminal_app.rs:869`, while visual selection is stored separately in `TerminalUi::visual_selection` and leaves `UiMode` as `Command` at `src/ui.rs:934`. Pressing an arrow key in visual mode therefore clears the selection via `src/ui.rs:459` before the later escape sequence becomes `UiKey::Left/Right/Up/Down`, so the visual movement handlers at `src/ui.rs:920` are unreachable from a real terminal. The existing harness does not catch this because `src/ui_harness.rs:89` parses complete escape sequences before byte dispatch. Evidence that would resolve this is a fix that defers ESC while `TerminalUi::has_visual_selection()` is true, plus a terminal-app or PTY test that sends raw arrow bytes during visual selection and verifies the yank range moves.

